t":null,"text":"RE model for subgroup (\n\n"},{"end_offset":6717,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000207","start_offset":6714,"table_hint":null,"text":"Q\n\n"},{"end_offset":6731,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000208","start_offset":6717,"table_hint":null,"text":"=3.87, df=5,\n\n"},{"end_offset":6734,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000209","start_offset":6731,"table_hint":null,"text":"P\n\n"},{"end_offset":6742,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000210","start_offset":6734,"table_hint":null,"text":"=0.57;\n\n"},{"end_offset":6745,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000211","start_offset":6742,"table_hint":null,"text":"I\n\n"},{"end_offset":6755,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000212","start_offset":6745,"table_hint":null,"text":"2 =0.0%,\n\n"},{"end_offset":6758,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000213","start_offset":6755,"table_hint":null,"text":"2\n\n"},{"end_offset":6766,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000214","start_offset":6758,"table_hint":null,"text":"=0.00)\n\n"},{"end_offset":7058,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000215","start_offset":6766,"table_hint":null,"text":"multiple (mostly small) randomised trials for delirium, and the limited available data on mortality. Hence, the hypothesis that dexmedetomidine may reduce delirium and mortality should be tested in a large RCT. The present results from this metaanalysis should not be considered definitive.\n\n"},{"end_offset":7948,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000216","start_offset":7058,"table_hint":null,"text":"We propose that 'days alive and at home ' would be a reasonable patient-centred outcome for such a study that captures meaningful morbidity (such as delirium) and mortality. 8 Given that delirium and mortality risk are elevated in older subjects, and secondary analysis of the 4000 patient SPICE III trial suggested a specific benefit of dexmedetomidine sedation in older, surgical, or both participants, 9 such a trial should focus on vulnerable older patients. We suggest that because of design limitations, current trial data do not address the important question of potential benefits of early perioperative administration of dexmedetomidine in cardiac surgical ICU patients. Future studies should address the potential benefit of sympatholytic, organ-protective dosing of dexmedetomidine during and after surgery, as intraoperative administration may offer particular benefits. 10,11\n\n"},{"end_offset":7974,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000217","start_offset":7948,"table_hint":null,"text":"Declarations of interest\n\n"},{"end_offset":8098,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000218","start_offset":7974,"table_hint":null,"text":"YS declares receiving speaker honorarium from Pfizer. RDS is a member of the board of the British Journal of Anaesthesia .\n\n"},{"end_offset":8166,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000219","start_offset":8098,"table_hint":null,"text":"The other authors declare that they have no conflicts of interest.\n\n"},{"end_offset":8175,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000220","start_offset":8166,"table_hint":null,"text":"Funding\n\n"},{"end_offset":8226,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000221","start_offset":8175,"table_hint":null,"text":"US National Institute on Aging (R01 AG063849-01).\n\n"},{"end_offset":8238,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000222","start_offset":8226,"table_hint":null,"text":"References\n\n"},{"end_offset":8432,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000223","start_offset":8238,"table_hint":null,"text":"Momeni M, Khalifa C, Lemaire G, et al. Propofol plus lowdose dexmedetomidine infusion and postoperative delirium in older patients undergoing cardiac surgery. Br J Anaesth 2021; 126 : 665 e 73\n\n"},{"end_offset":8633,"heading":null,"page":2,"segment_id":"S000224","start_offset":8432,"table_hint":null,"text":"Turan A, Duncan A, Leung S, et al. Dexmedetomidine for reduction of atrial fibrillation and delirium after cardiac surgery (DECADE): a 